      "math_academy_id": "q-148155",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=3,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=6,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=2.$ Find $\\text{Var}[4X+2Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[4X+2Y] & ={4}^{2}\\cdot 3+{2}^{2}\\cdot 6+2\\cdot 4\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =48+24+32 \\\\  & =104.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
